# repentogxm v0.1.2-alpha (DRAFT): the complete CMake option set of the combined
# test build of 2026-11-06 (link id rel:v0.1.2-alpha-int-test-on-20261106,
# eboot sha256 28e9e11dc08ee5cd784e019d1f4d1e37fe3e6bfd674a43a2ea743b5c4ccb2eb9).
# Every value equals that build's CMakeCache.txt; options are written with
# their declared type (the build passed them as STRING -D overrides). The set
# is the B-all2 lever set of 2026-10-26 (S1 recorder admission cache, S2
# attribute memo, S4 attribute batch, S5 fullspeed floor debt, S6 timeGetTime
# reciprocal, S8 binding replay, the Shader::Bind packet, the heap free
# prefilter pair, the fight SFX preload, Lua integer2str) plus six fixes:
# ISAAC_VITA_CXX_THROW_DIAG, ISAAC_VITA_INTRO_PLAY (issue #14),
# ISAAC_VITA_DISPLAY_CENTER_Y (issue #5, 5.8b),
# ISAAC_VITA_EFFECTS_PROFILE_KEEP_COLOR_MODIFIER, ISAAC_VITA_VITAGL_INTENSITY_TEXTURE
# (issue #4, 4.2) and ISAAC_VITA_LUA_LOADFILE_RETRY. It is a test build, not a
# release candidate: the combined set has not had a device session yet. Before
# tagging, turn OFF every lever that did not pass its device gate, build, and
# REPLACE this file with the shipped build's cache (release/README.md step 1);
# tools/release/check_release_recipe.py must then pass on both this file and
# that CMakeCache.txt. This DRAFT paragraph is dropped at the tag.
#
# Paths are per machine and are given on the command line. Reproduce the
# build from a fresh build directory (softfp VitaSDK, Ninja, Python 3.10+,
# requirements.txt installed):
#
#   export VITASDK=<vitasdk-softfp>; export PATH="$VITASDK/bin:$PATH"
#   GUEST_LEAF_INLINE=1 GUEST_FLOOR_THUNK_FASTPATH=1 GUEST_GPR_FLUSH_MASK=1 \
#     python tools/build_vita.py --pe <isaac-ng.exe.unpacked.exe> \
#       --vitasdk "$VITASDK" --generated-dir <generated> --generate-only
#   cmake -S recomp/vita -B <build> -G Ninja -C release/v0.1.2-alpha.cmake \
#     -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE="$VITASDK/share/vita.toolchain.cmake" \
#     -DISAAC_PE_PATH=<isaac-ng.exe.unpacked.exe> \
#     -DISAAC_GENERATED_DIR=<generated> \
#     -DISAAC_LUA53_SOURCE_DIR=<pristine lua-5.3.3 source tree> \
#     -DISAAC_VITA_THEORADEC_PREFIX=<libtheora 1.2.0 softfp prefix> \
#     -DISAAC_VITA_TROPHY_PACK_DIR=<ISAC00000_00..05/TROPHY.TRP dir>
#   ninja -C <build> eboot.bin the-binding-of-isaac-repentance.vpk
#
# The three GUEST_* variables select the generation-time switches the corpus
# was produced with (tiny-leaf inlining, the floor thunk fast path and the
# dirty-only GPR publication; the test build's corpus was generated with all
# three); a corpus generated without them does not match these options.
# THEORADEC_SOURCE=master needs a libtheora 1.2.0 prefix with its ARM/NEON
# assembly, built by the same softfp toolchain (recomp/vita/README.md,
# ISAAC_VITA_THEORADEC_SOURCE); TROPHIES=ON packages trophy packs only when
# TROPHY_PACK_DIR names them (they are game-derived and built locally, never
# committed: recomp/vita/TROPHIES.md). A -D on the command line overrides an entry of
# this file (release candidates override ISAAC_VITA_GUEST_LINK_ID).
# CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release is byte-neutral and keeps the raw allocator gate
# armed. SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH fixes the timestamps of the VPK members
# (2026-09-07 00:00:00 UTC, unchanged from v0.1.1-alpha).

